# Structure Pro

Next.js App Router, TypeScript, and Tailwind. The building scene uses React Three Fiber, Three.js, and `@react-three/drei`.

Feature code lives in `src/features/<feature>/`. Every feature has the same folders as CPQ: `components/`, `config/`, `db/`, `hooks/`, `locales/`, `server/`, `types/`, and `utils/`.

CRM views live in subfeatures under `src/features/crm/conversations/`, `src/features/crm/deals/`, `src/features/crm/customers/`, `src/features/crm/quotes/`, `src/features/crm/settings/`, and `src/features/crm/support/`. Each subfeature uses those same folders. Code shared by those views lives in `src/features/crm/common/`.

- Building options come from `src/features/cpq/config/catalog.json` through `src/features/cpq/utils/catalog.ts`.
- Prices come from `src/features/cpq/config/pricing.json` through `src/features/cpq/utils/pricing.ts`.
- Do not hardcode prices or dimensions in components.
- 3D scene elements live in `src/features/cpq/components/` with the other building UI.
- UI copy lives in `src/features/<feature>/locales/`.
